{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015ydd5bM64chxakRywucEvm","type":"tool_result","content":"# Implementation log\n\nOne entry per significant change, appended at the end. Each entry says what changed, what was learned and what is left. Agents add entries too (see AGENTS.md).\n\n## Notes from the harness build\n\n- Gates verified on macOS with Homebrew Ruby 4.0.0, SQLite3 and Node 25 (CI uses Node 20): `make check-fast` about 22 s (RuboCop 1099 files, Stylelint, 2888 unit tests), `make check` about 60 s (6064 tests plus the autoload test). Tests run with `PARALLEL_WORKERS` set to the CPU count; `test/test_helper.rb` pins 1 worker when the variable is absent.\n- No test was skipped or deleted. Without the `svn` binary, 28 tests fail (`test/functional/repositories_controller_test.rb`, `test/functional/sys_controller_test.rb`, `test/integration/api_test/repositories_test.rb`, `test/integration/api_test/issues_test.rb`, `test/unit/user_test.rb`), because they create `Repository::Subversion` records without the `scm_available` guard used in `test/unit/changeset_test.rb`. `svn` is now a documented prerequisite and `make setup` warns when it is missing.\n- The Makefile falls back to `/opt/homebrew/opt/ruby/bin` when the `ruby` on PATH is older than 3.3, and prefixes Ruby commands with `$(RUN)` because GNU Make 3.81 (macOS) ignores PATH changes for simple commands.\n- Left out of `make check`, still run by the existing workflows: system tests (`make test-system`, need Chrome and a Mermaid.js download), `bundle audit` (`make audit`, needs network), the PostgreSQL and MySQL jobs and the Ruby 3.3/3.4 matrix (`.github/workflows/tests.yml`).\n- Silent skips: SCM repository tests skip when `tmp/test` is empty (`make test-scm-setup` unpacks git, filesystem and subversion; CI unpacks all), and LDAP tests skip without an LDAP server. Locally, 43 unit tests and 64 tests overall were skipped. With the git, filesystem and subversion repositories unpacked, `make check` also passed in parallel (6228 runs, 61 skips), so parallel workers do not collide on the shared repositories in `tmp/test`. Bazaar, CVS and Mercurial were not tried locally (binaries missing); CI covers them.\n- `lib/tasks/ci.rake` and `config/database.yml.example` contain `jenkins`/`jenkins` database credentials for the upstream CI server. They are test credentials, not production secrets, and were left unchanged. The `uw-harness` secret scan also flags `config/locales/ja.yml`, `th.yml` and `zh.yml`: these are translations of the word \"password\", not secrets.\n- `uw-harness check` only sees the `default` task of the Rakefile, not `lib/tasks/*.rake`. Rake tasks that docs need are wrapped in Makefile targets (`make locales-update`, `make icons`, `make test-scm-setup`).\n\n## 2026-11-01: \"no test run\" report from uw-harness verify\n\n- What happened: `npx uw-harness verify` reported that `make check-fast` and `make check` passed but showed no test run. Both gates do run tests. Minitest prints `2978 runs, 12393 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 43 skips` (check-fast) and `6228 runs, 32959 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 61 skips`, `4 runs, ...` (Bazaar) and `1 runs, ...` (autoload) for check.\n- Cause: `parseTestSummary` in `uw-harness/src/gates.ts` knows pytest, unittest, Jest, Vitest, Surefire, Cargo, RSpec, PHPUnit, Mocha and Go, but not Minitest. Proposed rule: `^(\\d+) runs, (\\d+) assertions, (\\d+) failures, (\\d+) errors, (\\d+) skips` with ran = runs, skipped = skips, failed = failures + errors.\n- Decision: gates unchanged. No extra output was added to imitate another runner, and no reporter gem was added (dependency change). The fix belongs in the CLI.\n- The baseline message \"before the harness: the test command did not run tests (exit 1)\" is expected: the base commit has no `config/database.yml`, which `make setup` writes.\n- Left: re-run `uw-harness verify` once the CLI parses Minitest summaries.\n\n## 2026-11-01: second \"no test run\" report from uw-harness verify\n\n- What happened: verify round 2 reported again that `make check-fast` and `make check` show no test run. Re-ran `make check-fast` locally: it runs 2978 unit tests (`2978 runs, 12393 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 43 skips`, about 20 s), so the gates do run tests.\n- Cause, confirmed again in `uw-harness/src/gates.ts` (`parseTestSummary`): there is no rule for the Minitest summary line, which is the only summary format that `bin/rails test` prints. No other format in the parser can match Minitest output without printing fake output.\n- Decision: gates unchanged. Printing a pytest, unittest or RSpec style line to satisfy the parser would mislead the check, and adding a reporter gem (for example minitest-reporters) is a dependency change that this round does not allow. Reported in `blocked`.\n- Left: add a Minitest rule to `parseTestSummary` in uw-harness (`/^(\\d+) runs, (\\d+) assertions, (\\d+) failures, (\\d+) errors, (\\d+) skips/gm`, ran = runs, skipped = skips, failed = failures + errors), then re-run `npx uw-harness verify`.\n\n## 2026-11-01: third \"no test run\" report from uw-harness verify\n\n- What happened: verify round 3 reported the same thing for `make check-fast` and `make check`. Re-ran `make check-fast`: `Running 2978 tests in parallel using 14 processes`, then `2978 runs, 12393 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 43 skips` in about 15 s. The gates run tests.\n- Checked again: `parseTestSummary` in `uw-harness/src/gates.ts` (last change dc97cc0) still has no Minitest rule. The repo has no other test runner: `package.json` only has Stylelint, and the Gemfile has no Minitest reporter.\n- Decision: gates unchanged, for the same reasons as round 2 (no fake summary line, no new reporter gem). Reported in `blocked`.\n- Left: add the Minitest rule to uw-harness, then re-run `npx uw-harness verify`.\n\n## 2026-11-01: harness built by uw-harness 0.3.0 with claude\n\nScore 19 → 86, level 0 → 1.\n\nThe branch adds a root Makefile that wraps the existing bin/rails, bundle, rake and npx commands. make check-fast runs RuboCop, Stylelint and 2888 unit tests in about 22 s. make check runs 6064 tests plus the autoload test in about 60 s. Both pass from a clean shell. Tests run with PARALLEL_WORKERS set to the CPU count (unit tests: 15 s instead of 65 s), and the Makefile falls back to Homebrew Ruby when the system Ruby is older than 3.3, with a workaround for GNU Make 3.81. A new harness.yml workflow runs `npx -y uw-harness verify` on push and pull request, but the package is not on npm yet. Docs (architecture, product, ADRs, local-dev, deploy, observability), four skills, AGENTS.md, compose.yaml, .env.example, .tool-versions and a pre-push hook were added. The 10 open questions about deploy, observability, the local database and where changes go are TODO blocks.\n\nBoth gates already run tests (check-fast: 2978 Minitest runs; check: 6228 + 4 + 1 runs, all passing). The \"no test run\" failure is a false negative in the uw-harness CLI: parseTestSummary does not parse the Minitest summary line. Gates were not changed and no imitation output was added; the finding and a proposed parser regex are in blocked and in a new dated entry in docs/harness/log.md.\n\nRe-ran make check-fast: it passes and runs 2978 unit tests (Minitest summary '2978 runs, 12393 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 43 skips'). make check was not re-run this round; it passed with 6228 tests in the previous round. The 'no test run' report comes from uw-harness: parseTestSummary does not recognise Minitest output. Gates are unchanged, because printing fake output or adding a reporter gem would mislead the check or change dependencies. The cause and the proposed parser rule are recorded in docs/harness/log.md and reported in blocked.\n\nThird round of the same report. Re-ran make check-fast: it passes and runs 2978 unit tests (0 failures, 43 skips); make check runs the full non-system suite. The 'no test run' result comes from the uw-harness CLI, whose parseTestSummary still has no Minitest rule, so it cannot read Redmine's test output. Gates are unchanged; no fake output and no reporter dependency were added. Logged the round in docs/harness/log.md and reported the CLI fix in blocked.\n\n**Assessment.** Redmine is a flexible, self-hosted project management web application written with Ruby on Rails (README.rdoc). Stack: Ruby (>= 3.3, < 4.1; CI matrix 3.3, 3.4, 4.0), JavaScript (Stimulus controllers, legacy jQuery), ERB / RSB view templates, CSS, Perl (extra/svn/Redmine.pm), Python (Mercurial helper in lib/redmine/scm/adapters/mercurial), Ruby on Rails 8.1.4, Propshaft (assets), importmap-rails + stimulus-rails + requestjs-rails, Doorkeeper (OAuth2 provider), Minitest + Mocha + Capybara/Selenium (tests), RuboCop (rubocop-performance, rubocop-rails), Stylelint 16 (CSS lint, Node 20), Puma (development and system tests). The full assessment stays in `.git/uw-harness/assessment.md` on the machine that ran uw-harness.\n\nRisks seen before the harness:\n\n- config/database.yml is gitignored and the Gemfile decides which DB adapter gem to install from it: `bundle install` without that file installs no adapter and `bin/rails test` fails. The test command will not run on a fresh clone until setup writes config/database.yml.\n- Gemfile.lock and db/schema.rb are gitignored: dependency versions are resolved at install time, so installs are not reproducible and a new gem release can break the gates.\n- The full test suite (402 test files) is long; a fast gate that runs it all will be slow and agents may skip it. SCM and LDAP tests silently skip when tmp/test repositories or an LDAP server are missing, so a green run does not cover them.\n- System tests need Chrome/ChromeDriver and a Mermaid.js download from registry.npmjs.org; bundle audit needs network. These cannot be part of an offline gate.\n- Upstream development happens on redmine.org SVN; any harness files added here may conflict with upstream syncs, and CONTRIBUTING.md says GitHub PRs are not reviewed.\n\n**Before the harness**: `bin/rails test`, ran no test (exit 1).\n\n  ◐ L3 Production can be observed  docs/observability.md has open questions for a human\n\n  Capabilities\n  ✓ L2 Skills for repeated tasks  4 skills\n\n  Before  harness coverage 19/100  level 0 (not yet oriented)  3 pass, 1 partial, 15 missing\n  After   harness coverage 86/100  level 1 (oriented)  14 pass, 5 partial, 0 missing\n\n  ✗ Gates not verified: see docs/harness/log.md\n  ! 6 test files only compare literals (for example `assert True`) and protect nothing: extra/sample_plugin/test/integration/routing_test.rb, test/helpers/activities_helper_test.rb, test/system/quick_jump_test.rb\n  ! 7 files already in the repository hold secret-looking values: config/locales/ja.yml (password or secret), config/locales/th.yml (password or secret), config/locales/zh.yml (password or secret)\n  Committed the harness as dcf0ac026 on uw-harness/20261101-1617.\n\n  Findings and work left undone\n  - Gate \"fast\" (make check-fast) output must show a test run: The gate runs tests: a fresh run printed 'Running 2978 tests in parallel using 14 processes' and '2978 runs, 12393 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 43 skips' (exit 0). The CLI cannot see it because parseTestSummary in uw-harness/src/gates.ts (last change dc97cc0) has no rule for the Minitest summary line, the only format that bin/rails test prints. Fix belongs in the CLI: add /^(\\d+) runs, (\\d+) assertions, (\\d+) failures, (\\d+) errors, (\\d+) skips/gm with ran = runs, skipped = skips, failed = failures + errors. Printing a fake pytest/RSpec line would mislead the check, and adding a reporter gem (minitest-reporters) is a dependency change that is not allowed.\n  - Gate \"full\" (make check) output must show a test run: Same cause: make check runs all non-system tests (about 6228 runs), the Bazaar test and the autoload test, all reported with Minitest summary lines ('N runs, N assertions, N failures, N errors, N skips') that uw-harness parseTestSummary does not recognise. No other test runner exists in the repo (package.json has only Stylelint). Needs the Minitest rule in the CLI, then a re-run of npx uw-harness verify.\n\n  Next steps\n  1. Read docs/harness/brief.md, then review the branch: git log master..uw-harness/20261101-1617\n  2. Answer the open questions: search for \"uw-harness:todo\" in docs/\n  3. Prove the harness on one real task: npx uw-harness prove\n     Guard Subversion-dependent tests with scm_available\n     Five test files create Repository::Subversion records without the `skip \"Subversion is unavailable\" unless Repository::Subversion.scm_available` guard that test/unit/changeset_test.rb already uses, so 28 tests fail with 'Validation failed: Type is invalid' on a machine without svn. Add the guard to the affected tests (test/unit/user_test.rb:479, test/functional/repositories_controller_test.rb, test/functional/sys_controller_test.rb, test/integration/api_test/repositories_test.rb, test/integration/api_test/issues_test.rb:523) so the suite skips them instead of failing.\n     - Done when: With svn removed from PATH, `make check` reports 0 failures and 0 errors, and the affected tests appear as skips.\n     - Done when: With svn present, `make check` reports the same number of runs as before (6064 without SCM repositories) and 0 skipped tests are added.\n     - Done when: Only files under test/ are changed; make check-fast passes and a dated entry is added to docs/harness/log.md.\n  4. Push the branch and open a pull request. CI should run `npx uw-harness verify`.\n\n  Done in 36m 30s. Agent transcripts: /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/redmine/repo/.git/uw-harness\nrun exit 1\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/redmine/repo","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98c9b43a-1aa1-4043-94cd-7a9dd1b3395e","uuid":"ee2ed2c6-f2d1-4434-9e9a-dc379a47d0e5","timestamp":"2026-11-01T15:54:04.882Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Implementation log\n\nOne entry per significant change, appended at the end. Each entry says what changed, what was learned and what is left. Agents add entries too (see AGENTS.md).\n\n## Notes from the harness build\n\n- Gates verified on macOS with Homebrew Ruby 4.0.0, SQLite3 and Node 25 (CI uses Node 20): `make check-fast` about 22 s (RuboCop 1099 files, Stylelint, 2888 unit tests), `make check` about 60 s (6064 tests plus the autoload test). Tests run with `PARALLEL_WORKERS` set to the CPU count; `test/test_helper.rb` pins 1 worker when the variable is absent.\n- No test was skipped or deleted. Without the `svn` binary, 28 tests fail (`test/functional/repositories_controller_test.rb`, `test/functional/sys_controller_test.rb`, `test/integration/api_test/repositories_test.rb`, `test/integration/api_test/issues_test.rb`, `test/unit/user_test.rb`), because they create `Repository::Subversion` records without the `scm_available` guard used in `test/unit/changeset_test.rb`. `svn` is now a documented prerequisite and `make setup` warns when it is missing.\n- The Makefile falls back to `/opt/homebrew/opt/ruby/bin` when the `ruby` on PATH is older than 3.3, and prefixes Ruby commands with `$(RUN)` because GNU Make 3.81 (macOS) ignores PATH changes for simple commands.\n- Left out of `make check`, still run by the existing workflows: system tests (`make test-system`, need Chrome and a Mermaid.js download), `bundle audit` (`make audit`, needs network), the PostgreSQL and MySQL jobs and the Ruby 3.3/3.4 matrix (`.github/workflows/tests.yml`).\n- Silent skips: SCM repository tests skip when `tmp/test` is empty (`make test-scm-setup` unpacks git, filesystem and subversion; CI unpacks all), and LDAP tests skip without an LDAP server. Locally, 43 unit tests and 64 tests overall were skipped. With the git, filesystem and subversion repositories unpacked, `make check` also passed in parallel (6228 runs, 61 skips), so parallel workers do not collide on the shared repositories in `tmp/test`. Bazaar, CVS and Mercurial were not tried locally (binaries missing); CI covers them.\n- `lib/tasks/ci.rake` and `config/database.yml.example` contain `jenkins`/`jenkins` database credentials for the upstream CI server. They are test credentials, not production secrets, and were left unchanged. The `uw-harness` secret scan also flags `config/locales/ja.yml`, `th.yml` and `zh.yml`: these are translations of the word \"password\", not secrets.\n- `uw-harness check` only sees the `default` task of the Rakefile, not `lib/tasks/*.rake`. Rake tasks that docs need are wrapped in Makefile targets (`make locales-update`, `make icons`, `make test-scm-setup`).\n\n## 2026-11-01: \"no test run\" report from uw-harness verify\n\n- What happened: `npx uw-harness verify` reported that `make check-fast` and `make check` passed but showed no test run. Both gates do run tests. Minitest prints `2978 runs, 12393 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 43 skips` (check-fast) and `6228 runs, 32959 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 61 skips`, `4 runs, ...` (Bazaar) and `1 runs, ...` (autoload) for check.\n- Cause: `parseTestSummary` in `uw-harness/src/gates.ts` knows pytest, unittest, Jest, Vitest, Surefire, Cargo, RSpec, PHPUnit, Mocha and Go, but not Minitest. Proposed rule: `^(\\d+) runs, (\\d+) assertions, (\\d+) failures, (\\d+) errors, (\\d+) skips` with ran = runs, skipped = skips, failed = failures + errors.\n- Decision: gates unchanged. No extra output was added to imitate another runner, and no reporter gem was added (dependency change). The fix belongs in the CLI.\n- The baseline message \"before the harness: the test command did not run tests (exit 1)\" is expected: the base commit has no `config/database.yml`, which `make setup` writes.\n- Left: re-run `uw-harness verify` once the CLI parses Minitest summaries.\n\n## 2026-11-01: second \"no test run\" report from uw-harness verify\n\n- What happened: verify round 2 reported again that `make check-fast` and `make check` show no test run. Re-ran `make check-fast` locally: it runs 2978 unit tests (`2978 runs, 12393 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 43 skips`, about 20 s), so the gates do run tests.\n- Cause, confirmed again in `uw-harness/src/gates.ts` (`parseTestSummary`): there is no rule for the Minitest summary line, which is the only summary format that `bin/rails test` prints. No other format in the parser can match Minitest output without printing fake output.\n- Decision: gates unchanged. Printing a pytest, unittest or RSpec style line to satisfy the parser would mislead the check, and adding a reporter gem (for example minitest-reporters) is a dependency change that this round does not allow. Reported in `blocked`.\n- Left: add a Minitest rule to `parseTestSummary` in uw-harness (`/^(\\d+) runs, (\\d+) assertions, (\\d+) failures, (\\d+) errors, (\\d+) skips/gm`, ran = runs, skipped = skips, failed = failures + errors), then re-run `npx uw-harness verify`.\n\n## 2026-11-01: third \"no test run\" report from uw-harness verify\n\n- What happened: verify round 3 reported the same thing for `make check-fast` and `make check`. Re-ran `make check-fast`: `Running 2978 tests in parallel using 14 processes`, then `2978 runs, 12393 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 43 skips` in about 15 s. The gates run tests.\n- Checked again: `parseTestSummary` in `uw-harness/src/gates.ts` (last change dc97cc0) still has no Minitest rule. The repo has no other test runner: `package.json` only has Stylelint, and the Gemfile has no Minitest reporter.\n- Decision: gates unchanged, for the same reasons as round 2 (no fake summary line, no new reporter gem). Reported in `blocked`.\n- Left: add the Minitest rule to uw-harness, then re-run `npx uw-harness verify`.\n\n## 2026-11-01: harness built by uw-harness 0.3.0 with claude\n\nScore 19 → 86, level 0 → 1.\n\nThe branch adds a root Makefile that wraps the existing bin/rails, bundle, rake and npx commands. make check-fast runs RuboCop, Stylelint and 2888 unit tests in about 22 s. make check runs 6064 tests plus the autoload test in about 60 s. Both pass from a clean shell. Tests run with PARALLEL_WORKERS set to the CPU count (unit tests: 15 s instead of 65 s), and the Makefile falls back to Homebrew Ruby when the system Ruby is older than 3.3, with a workaround for GNU Make 3.81. A new harness.yml workflow runs `npx -y uw-harness verify` on push and pull request, but the package is not on npm yet. Docs (architecture, product, ADRs, local-dev, deploy, observability), four skills, AGENTS.md, compose.yaml, .env.example, .tool-versions and a pre-push hook were added. The 10 open questions about deploy, observability, the local database and where changes go are TODO blocks.\n\nBoth gates already run tests (check-fast: 2978 Minitest runs; check: 6228 + 4 + 1 runs, all passing). The \"no test run\" failure is a false negative in the uw-harness CLI: parseTestSummary does not parse the Minitest summary line. Gates were not changed and no imitation output was added; the finding and a proposed parser regex are in blocked and in a new dated entry in docs/harness/log.md.\n\nRe-ran make check-fast: it passes and runs 2978 unit tests (Minitest summary '2978 runs, 12393 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 43 skips'). make check was not re-run this round; it passed with 6228 tests in the previous round. The 'no test run' report comes from uw-harness: parseTestSummary does not recognise Minitest output. Gates are unchanged, because printing fake output or adding a reporter gem would mislead the check or change dependencies. The cause and the proposed parser rule are recorded in docs/harness/log.md and reported in blocked.\n\nThird round of the same report. Re-ran make check-fast: it passes and runs 2978 unit tests (0 failures, 43 skips); make check runs the full non-system suite. The 'no test run' result comes from the uw-harness CLI, whose parseTestSummary still has no Minitest rule, so it cannot read Redmine's test output. Gates are unchanged; no fake output and no reporter dependency were added. Logged the round in docs/harness/log.md and reported the CLI fix in blocked.\n\n**Assessment.** Redmine is a flexible, self-hosted project management web application written with Ruby on Rails (README.rdoc). Stack: Ruby (>= 3.3, < 4.1; CI matrix 3.3, 3.4, 4.0), JavaScript (Stimulus controllers, legacy jQuery), ERB / RSB view templates, CSS, Perl (extra/svn/Redmine.pm), Python (Mercurial helper in lib/redmine/scm/adapters/mercurial), Ruby on Rails 8.1.4, Propshaft (assets), importmap-rails + stimulus-rails + requestjs-rails, Doorkeeper (OAuth2 provider), Minitest + Mocha + Capybara/Selenium (tests), RuboCop (rubocop-performance, rubocop-rails), Stylelint 16 (CSS lint, Node 20), Puma (development and system tests). The full assessment stays in `.git/uw-harness/assessment.md` on the machine that ran uw-harness.\n\nRisks seen before the harness:\n\n- config/database.yml is gitignored and the Gemfile decides which DB adapter gem to install from it: `bundle install` without that file installs no adapter and `bin/rails test` fails. The test command will not run on a fresh clone until setup writes config/database.yml.\n- Gemfile.lock and db/schema.rb are gitignored: dependency versions are resolved at install time, so installs are not reproducible and a new gem release can break the gates.\n- The full test suite (402 test files) is long; a fast gate that runs it all will be slow and agents may skip it. SCM and LDAP tests silently skip when tmp/test repositories or an LDAP server are missing, so a green run does not cover them.\n- System tests need Chrome/ChromeDriver and a Mermaid.js download from registry.npmjs.org; bundle audit needs network. These cannot be part of an offline gate.\n- Upstream development happens on redmine.org SVN; any harness files added here may conflict with upstream syncs, and CONTRIBUTING.md says GitHub PRs are not reviewed.\n\n**Before the harness**: `bin/rails test`, ran no test (exit 1).\n\n  ◐ L3 Production can be observed  docs/observability.md has open questions for a human\n\n  Capabilities\n  ✓ L2 Skills for repeated tasks  4 skills\n\n  Before  harness coverage 19/100  level 0 (not yet oriented)  3 pass, 1 partial, 15 missing\n  After   harness coverage 86/100  level 1 (oriented)  14 pass, 5 partial, 0 missing\n\n  ✗ Gates not verified: see docs/harness/log.md\n  ! 6 test files only compare literals (for example `assert True`) and protect nothing: extra/sample_plugin/test/integration/routing_test.rb, test/helpers/activities_helper_test.rb, test/system/quick_jump_test.rb\n  ! 7 files already in the repository hold secret-looking values: config/locales/ja.yml (password or secret), config/locales/th.yml (password or secret), config/locales/zh.yml (password or secret)\n  Committed the harness as dcf0ac026 on uw-harness/20261101-1617.\n\n  Findings and work left undone\n  - Gate \"fast\" (make check-fast) output must show a test run: The gate runs tests: a fresh run printed 'Running 2978 tests in parallel using 14 processes' and '2978 runs, 12393 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 43 skips' (exit 0). The CLI cannot see it because parseTestSummary in uw-harness/src/gates.ts (last change dc97cc0) has no rule for the Minitest summary line, the only format that bin/rails test prints. Fix belongs in the CLI: add /^(\\d+) runs, (\\d+) assertions, (\\d+) failures, (\\d+) errors, (\\d+) skips/gm with ran = runs, skipped = skips, failed = failures + errors. Printing a fake pytest/RSpec line would mislead the check, and adding a reporter gem (minitest-reporters) is a dependency change that is not allowed.\n  - Gate \"full\" (make check) output must show a test run: Same cause: make check runs all non-system tests (about 6228 runs), the Bazaar test and the autoload test, all reported with Minitest summary lines ('N runs, N assertions, N failures, N errors, N skips') that uw-harness parseTestSummary does not recognise. No other test runner exists in the repo (package.json has only Stylelint). Needs the Minitest rule in the CLI, then a re-run of npx uw-harness verify.\n\n  Next steps\n  1. Read docs/harness/brief.md, then review the branch: git log master..uw-harness/20261101-1617\n  2. Answer the open questions: search for \"uw-harness:todo\" in docs/\n  3. Prove the harness on one real task: npx uw-harness prove\n     Guard Subversion-dependent tests with scm_available\n     Five test files create Repository::Subversion records without the `skip \"Subversion is unavailable\" unless Repository::Subversion.scm_available` guard that test/unit/changeset_test.rb already uses, so 28 tests fail with 'Validation failed: Type is invalid' on a machine without svn. Add the guard to the affected tests (test/unit/user_test.rb:479, test/functional/repositories_controller_test.rb, test/functional/sys_controller_test.rb, test/integration/api_test/repositories_test.rb, test/integration/api_test/issues_test.rb:523) so the suite skips them instead of failing.\n     - Done when: With svn removed from PATH, `make check` reports 0 failures and 0 errors, and the affected tests appear as skips.\n     - Done when: With svn present, `make check` reports the same number of runs as before (6064 without SCM repositories) and 0 skipped tests are added.\n     - Done when: Only files under test/ are changed; make check-fast passes and a dated entry is added to docs/harness/log.md.\n  4. Push the branch and open a pull request. CI should run `npx uw-harness verify`.\n\n  Done in 36m 30s. Agent transcripts: /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/redmine/repo/.git/uw-harness\nrun exit 1","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/redmine/repo","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015ydd5bM64chxakRywucEvm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"