{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcV6CqmjaossDbdXpKFD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J84YCe8c7KvMgkeYHArR5t","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/redmine/repo\ncat > docs/decisions/0001-record-architecture-decisions.md <<'EOF'\n# 0001. Record architecture decisions\n\n- Status: accepted\n- Date: 2026-11-01\n\n## Context\n\nRedmine is about twenty years old. Many choices (database support, the asset pipeline, how plugins load) are visible in the code but the reasons are only in issues on www.redmine.org. Agents and new contributors need the reasons next to the code.\n\n## Decision\n\nWe keep one short Markdown file per decision in `docs/decisions/`, numbered `NNNN-title-in-kebab-case.md`. Each file has three sections:\n\n- **Context**: the problem and the forces at play.\n- **Decision**: what we chose, in one or two paragraphs.\n- **Consequences**: what gets easier, what gets harder, what to watch.\n\nA record that was reconstructed from the code says so in its status line: \"Inferred from the code, to be confirmed by the team.\" A decision that changes replaces the old record with a new one; the old record gets the status \"superseded by NNNN\".\n\n## Consequences\n\n- A change that makes or reverses an architectural choice adds a record in the same change.\n- Records are short. Detail stays in the code, in `docs/architecture.md` or in the linked redmine.org issue.\nEOF\ncat > docs/decisions/0002-multi-database-support-via-database-yml.md <<'EOF'\n# 0002. Support several databases, chosen in config/database.yml\n\n- Status: inferred from the code, to be confirmed by the team\n- Date: 2026-11-01\n\n## Context\n\nRedmine is self-hosted. Each organization runs it on the database it already operates: MySQL or MariaDB, PostgreSQL, SQLite3 or SQL Server.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe application supports all four through ActiveRecord. `config/database.yml` (ignored by git, examples in `config/database.yml.example`) names the adapter. The `Gemfile` reads that file and installs only the adapter gems it finds (`mysql2` or `trilogy`, `pg`, `sqlite3`, `tiny_tds` with `activerecord-sqlserver-adapter`). CI runs the test suite on PostgreSQL 14, MySQL 8.4 and SQLite3 (`.github/workflows/tests.yml`).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `config/database.yml` must exist before `bundle install`. Without it, no adapter gem is installed and nothing can run. `bin/harness setup` writes a SQLite3 file when none exists.\n- Migrations and SQL in models must work on every adapter. Code that is adapter-specific checks `Redmine::Database` (`lib/redmine/database.rb`).\n- The harness gates use SQLite3 only. PostgreSQL and MySQL are covered by `.github/workflows/tests.yml`, or locally with `compose.yaml`.\nEOF\ncat > docs/decisions/0003-importmap-stimulus-without-js-build.md <<'EOF'\n# 0003. Serve JavaScript with importmap and Stimulus, without a build step\n\n- Status: inferred from the code, to be confirmed by the team\n- Date: 2026-11-01\n\n## Context\n\nAdministrators install Redmine from a source archive (`doc/INSTALL`). A Node.js build step would add a toolchain to every installation.\n\n## Decision\n\nJavaScript is written as Stimulus controllers in `app/javascript/controllers` and served as ES modules through `importmap-rails` (`config/importmap.rb`) and Propshaft. Third-party modules are vendored in `vendor/javascript`. Node.js is used only in development, for Stylelint (`package.json`).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- No bundler, transpiler or `node_modules` is needed in production.\n- New JavaScript must be plain browser-ready ES modules.\n- Large optional libraries are installed on demand, for example Mermaid.js with `bin/rails redmine:mermaid:install`.\nEOF\nls lib/redmine/database.rb; grep -n \"def \\|module\" lib/redmine/database.rb | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3543,"cache_read_input_tokens":109807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3543},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98c9b43a-1aa1-4043-94cd-7a9dd1b3395e","uuid":"d47c611f-0e5e-4fad-a523-61472e59cab1","timestamp":"2026-11-01T15:59:18.074Z","request_id":"req_011CgcV6CdcZXuc7exvJ4tQ6","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01J84YCe8c7KvMgkeYHArR5t":{"command":"cd /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/redmine/repo\ncat > docs/decisions/0001-record-architecture-decisions.md <<'EOF'\n# 0001. Record architecture decisions\n\n- Status: accepted\n- Date: 2026-11-01\n\n## Context\n\nRedmine is about twenty years old. Many choices (database support, the asset pipeline, how plugins load) are visible in the code but the reasons are only in issues on www.redmine.org. Agents and new contributors need the reasons next to the code.\n\n## Decision\n\nWe keep one short Markdown file per decision in `docs/decisions/`, numbered `NNNN-title-in-kebab-case.md`. Each file has three sections:\n\n- **Context**: the problem and the forces at play.\n- **Decision**: what we chose, in one or two paragraphs.\n- **Consequences**: what gets easier, what gets harder, what to watch.\n\nA record that was reconstructed from the code says so in its status line: \"Inferred from the code, to be confirmed by the team.\" A decision that changes replaces the old record with a new one; the old record gets the status \"superseded by NNNN\".\n\n## Consequences\n\n- A change that makes or reverses an architectural choice adds a record in the same change.\n- Records are short. Detail stays in the code, in `docs/architecture.md` or in the linked redmine.org issue.\nEOF\ncat > docs/decisions/0002-multi-database-support-via-database-yml.md <<'EOF'\n# 0002