{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcVSZx5LYa7JtSb8nZe5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014YepJnKjwmb9jZo2gZweo1","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/redmine/repo/docs/harness/log.md","old_string":"- On the first `bin/harness setup`, `db:prepare` on the development database failed once at migration 72 (`AddEnumerationsPosition`). The second run and a run on a fresh database passed; the cause was not found.","new_string":"- Finding: on a new SQLite3 database, `bin/rails db:prepare` fails every time at migration 072 (`db/migrate/072_add_enumerations_position.rb`) with `no such column: enumerations.position`. The migration skips `add_column` when `Enumeration.column_names` already lists `position`, so stale column information makes it fail. `bin/rails db:create db:migrate` passes every time (CI uses it too, through `ci:setup`). `bin/harness setup` therefore uses `db:create db:migrate`. The migration was not changed; a human should decide whether to fix it upstream."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1024,"cache_read_input_tokens":143801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1024},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98c9b43a-1aa1-4043-94cd-7a9dd1b3395e","uuid":"effcafc2-953c-46c0-9893-77fb1ecf9b75","timestamp":"2026-11-01T16:03:44.005Z","request_id":"req_011CgcVSZX2Uz1FDyeLUpYM1","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014YepJnKjwmb9jZo2gZweo1":{"file_path":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/redmine/repo/docs/harness/log.md","old_string":"- On the first `bin/harness setup`, `db:prepare` on the development database failed once at migration 72 (`AddEnumerationsPosition`). The second run and a run on a fresh database passed; the cause was not found.","new_string":"- Finding: on a new SQLite3 database, `bin/rails db:prepare` fails every time at migration 072 (`db/migrate/072_add_enumerations_position.rb`) with `no such column: enumerations.position`. The migration skips `add_column` when `Enumeration.column_names` already lists `position`, so stale column information makes it fail. `bin/rails db:create db:migrate` passes every time (CI uses it too, through `ci:setup`). `bin/harness setup` therefore uses `db:create db:migrate`. The migration was not changed; a human should decide whether to fix it upstream."}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014YepJnKjwmb9jZo2gZweo1","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/redmine/repo/docs/harness/log.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98c9b43a-1aa1-4043-94cd-7a9dd1b3395e","uuid":"db3ffa51-3f56-4304-9e28-5f1d6ef14775","timestamp":"2026-11-01T16:03:44.014Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/redmine/repo/docs/harness/log.md","oldString":"- On the first `bin/harness setup`, `db:prepare` on the development database failed once at migration 72 (`AddEnumerationsPosition`). The second run and a run on a fresh database passed; the cause was not found.","newString":"- Finding: on a new SQLite3 database, `bin/rails db:prepare` fails every time at migration 072 (`db/migrate/072_add_enumerations_position.rb`) with `no such column: enumerations.position`. The migration skips `add_column` when `Enumeration.column_names` already lists `position`, so stale column information makes it fail. `bin/rails db:create db:migrate` passes every time (CI uses it too, through `ci:setup`). `bin/harness setup` therefore uses `db:create db:migrate`. The migration was not changed; a human should decide whether to fix it upstream.","originalFile":"# Implementation log\n\nOne entry per significant change, appended at the end: date, what changed, what was learned, what is left.\n\n## Notes from the harness build\n\n- The gates were verified on macOS with Homebrew Ruby 4.0.0, SQLite3, Node 25 and `svn` installed. `bin/harness check-fast` took about 40 s (RuboCop on 1099 files, Stylelint, 3383 unit and helper tests, 0 failures, 92 skips). `bin/harness check` took about 3 minutes (6296 tests, 0 failures, 131 skips, plus 1 autoload test).\n- The harness tasks are in the root `Rakefile` and not in `lib/tasks/harness.rake`, because `uw-harness` reads task names only from the `Rakefile`. Unlike `lib/tasks/`, the `Rakefile` is inspected by RuboCop, so every harness task depends on `:environment` (cop `Rails/RakeEnvironment`). That costs about one second per task; the Rails environment loads without a database.\n- `bin/harness` exists because the `Rakefile` loads Rails: `rake` cannot run before `config/database.yml` exists and gems are installed. It also falls back to `/opt/homebrew/opt/ruby/bin` (or `/usr/local/opt/ruby/bin`) when the Ruby on PATH is older than 3.3, as on macOS.\n- Left out of `bin/harness check`, still run by the upstream workflows: system tests (`bin/harness test-system`, need Chrome and a Mermaid.js download), the Bazaar non-ASCII test (needs the `en_US.ISO8859-1` locale), `bundle audit` (needs network), the PostgreSQL and MySQL jobs and the Ruby 3.3 and 3.4 matrix (`.github/workflows/tests.yml`, `.github/workflows/linters.yml`).\n- No test was skipped or deleted by the harness. Skips come from the tests themselves: Mercurial, Bazaar and CVS tests skip when their binaries are missing, and LDAP tests skip without an LDAP server.\n- On the first `bin/harness setup`, `db:prepare` on the development database failed once at migration 72 (`AddEnumerationsPosition`). The second run and a run on a fresh database passed; the cause was not found.\n- `.tool-versions` pins Ruby 4.0.0 (the version the gates were verified with, also in the CI matrix) and Node.js 20 (the CI version). `.ruby-version` is ignored by git upstream, so it was not used.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":9,"oldLines":5,"newStart":9,"newLines":5,"lines":[" - `bin/harness` exists because the `Rakefile` loads Rails: `rake` cannot run before `config/database.yml` exists and gems are installed. It also falls back to `/opt/homebrew/opt/ruby/bin` (or `/usr/local/opt/ruby/bin`) when the Ruby on PATH is older than 3.3, as on macOS."," - Left out of `bin/harness check`, still run by the upstream workflows: system tests (`bin/harness test-system`, need Chrome and a Mermaid.js download), the Bazaar non-ASCII test (needs the `en_US.ISO8859-1` locale), `bundle audit` (needs network), the PostgreSQL and MySQL jobs and the Ruby 3.3 and 3.4 matrix (`.github/workflows/tests.yml`, `.github/workflows/linters.yml`)."," - No test was skipped or deleted by the harness. Skips come from the tests themselves: Mercurial, Bazaar and CVS tests skip when their binaries are missing, and LDAP tests skip without an LDAP server.","-- On the first `bin/harness setup`, `db:prepare` on the development database failed once at migration 72 (`AddEnumerationsPosition`). The second run and a run on a fresh database passed; the cause was not found.","+- Finding: on a new SQLite3 database, `bin/rails db:prepare` fails every time at migration 072 (`db/migrate/072_add_enumerations_position.rb`) with `no such column: enumerations.position`. The migration skips `add_column` when `Enumeration.column_names` already lists `position`, so stale column information makes it fail. `bin/rails db:create db:migrate` passes every time (CI uses it too, through `ci:setup`). `bin/harness setup` therefore uses `db:create db:migrate`. The migration was not changed; a human should decide whether to fix it upstream."," - `.tool-versions` pins Ruby 4.0.0 (the version the gates were verified with, also in the CI matrix) and Node.js 20 (the CI version). `.ruby-version` is ignored by git upstream, so it was not used."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014YepJnKjwmb9jZo2gZweo1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
