{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcVY7KrhMfYj8UACLAYt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VDuG7NwixSF2fa7w6uYt2A","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"changes":[{"path":"Rakefile","requirement":"task-runner","summary":"Kept the upstream lines. Added the harness tasks help, setup, dev, lint, check-fast, check and test-system to the root Rakefile, because uw-harness reads task names only from that file. They wrap bin/rails, RuboCop and Stylelint, and each depends on :environment so that RuboCop stays clean."},{"path":"bin/harness","requirement":"fast-gate","summary":"New wrapper. It picks a Ruby >= 3.3 and < 4.1, falling back to Homebrew Ruby when /usr/bin/ruby is too old. For setup it writes a SQLite3 config/database.yml if missing and runs bundle install and yarn install. Then it runs bundle exec rake <task>."},{"path":".github/workflows/harness.yml","requirement":"ci","summary":"New workflow on pull_request and on push to master: Ruby 4.0, Node 20, svn and hg, then npx -y uw-harness verify. Upstream tests.yml and linters.yml are unchanged."},{"path":".githooks/pre-push","requirement":"hooks","summary":"Pre-push hook that runs bin/harness check-fast. rake setup installs it with git config core.hooksPath .githooks."},{"path":"compose.yaml","requirement":"local-env","summary":"Optional PostgreSQL 14 and MySQL 8.4 services, the same as in tests.yml. The default setup uses SQLite3 and needs neither."},{"path":"docs/local-dev.md","requirement":"local-env","summary":"Prerequisites, first run, daily run, other databases, reset, debug and common problems. Also TODOs on the default database and on the tests the gates skip."},{"path":".env.example","requirement":"env-example","summary":"Lists every environment variable that the code, tests and Rake tasks read, with safe values. It also points to the git-ignored YAML config files and their .example templates."},{"path":".tool-versions","requirement":"toolchain-pinned","summary":"ruby 4.0.0 (the version the gates were verified with, also in the CI matrix) and nodejs 20 (the CI version)."},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","requirement":"architecture","summary":"The Mermaid diagram, then one section per component with folders, tech, key tables and the /up health route. Also lists what the repository does not show."},{"path":"docs/product.md","requirement":"product","summary":"Value proposition, user roles, 10 use cases with their code entry points, and a glossary."},{"path":"docs/decisions/0001-record-architecture-decisions.md","requirement":"decisions","summary":"The ADR format: context, decision, consequences, plus how to mark inferred records."},{"path":"docs/decisions/0002-multi-database-support-via-database-yml.md","requirement":"decisions","summary":"Inferred ADR: several databases are supported, and the Gemfile installs the adapter gems named in config/database.yml."},{"path":"docs/decisions/0003-importmap-stimulus-without-js-build.md","requirement":"decisions","summary":"Inferred ADR: Stimulus with importmap and Propshaft, no JavaScript build step."},{"path":"docs/agreements/working-agreements.md","requirement":"agreements","summary":"Branch and commit style taken from the git history, rules for agents, and a definition of done that includes the fast gate. Also TODOs on the contribution process and on the CI workflow."},{"path":"docs/deploy.md","requirement":"deploy-explicit","summary":"Summary of doc/INSTALL and doc/UPGRADING: environments, build, deploy, rollback and checks after a deploy. Two TODO blocks for what the repository does not show."},{"path":"docs/observability.md","requirement":"observability","summary":"Rails logger, log level and destinations, GET /up, the Admin > Information checklist, and how to tell that something is wrong. One TODO on production logs, error tracking and alerts."},{"path":"docs/harness/log.md","requirement":"implementation-log","summary":"Log header plus 'Notes from the harness build': gate timings, why the tasks are in the Rakefile, checks left out, the source of skipped tests, and the migration 072 / db:prepare finding."},{"path":".agents/skills/implement-change/SKILL.md","requirement":"skills","summary":"From task to verified change: find code and tests, run one test, check-fast, check, commit style, log entry."},{"path":".agents/skills/debug-local/SKILL.md","requirement":"skills","summary":"Reproduce, logs, debugger breakpoints, console and fixtures, SCM/LDAP skips, seeds, plugins."},{"path":".agents/skills/write-migration/SKILL.md","requirement":"skills","summary":"Portable migrations across SQLite3, PostgreSQL, MySQL and SQL Server: migrate, rollback, fixtures, compose databases."},{"path":".agents/skills/frontend-stimulus/SKILL.md","requirement":"skills","summary":"Stimulus controllers, importmap pins, CSS with open-color variables, sprite_icon and icons:generate, Stylelint, system tests."},{"path":".claude/skills","requirement":"skills","summary":"Relative symlink to ../.agents/skills."},{"path":"AGENTS.md","requirement":"agents-file","summary":"69-line index: what Redmine is, commands, layout, conventions, how to verify (check-fast before done, log entry), what never to do, links to docs and skills."},{"path":"CLAUDE.md","requirement":"agents-file","summary":"Symlink to AGENTS.md."}],"gates":{"setup":"bin/harness setup","fast":"bin/harness check-fast","full":"bin/harness check"},"todos":[{"requirement":"deploy-explicit","question":"Is this copy of Redmine deployed anywhere by your team (which server, which environments), or is it only a mirror of upstream used for development?","file":"docs/deploy.md"},{"requirement":"deploy-explicit","question":"If this copy is deployed: who can deploy, how is a release built for it (git tag, archive, branch), and how do you roll back a release that ran database migrations?","file":"docs/deploy.md"},{"requirement":"observability","question":"Where do production logs go (log/production.log, STDOUT to a collector?), and is there any error tracker, dashboard or alert channel for this instance?","file":"docs/observability.md"},{"requirement":"agreements","question":"Should changes from agents follow the upstream process (a patch attached to an issue on www.redmine.org, commit message ending with (#issue)) or a local branch and pull request process in this repository?","file":"docs/agreements/working-agreements.md"},{"requirement":"ci","question":"May the new workflow .github/workflows/harness.yml run on pull requests in this repository, given that upstream development happens in Subversion on www.redmine.org and GitHub pull requests are not reviewed there?","file":"docs/agreements/working-agreements.md"},{"requirement":"fast-gate","question":"Is it acceptable that the fast gate skips the SCM, LDAP and system (Chrome) tests that need external binaries or services?","file":"docs/local-dev.md"},{"requirement":"local-env","question":"Which database should be the default for local development and the gates: SQLite3 (the current default of bin/harness setup) or PostgreSQL/MySQL in Docker?","file":"docs/local-dev.md"}],"blocked":[{"requirement":"local-env","reason":"On a new SQLite3 database, bin/rails db:prepare fails every time at db/migrate/072_add_enumerations_position.rb (no such column: enumerations.position). The migration skips add_column when Enumeration.column_names already lists the column. bin/harness setup uses db:create db:migrate instead, which passes every time. The migration was not changed: a human should decide whether to fix it upstream."},{"requirement":"env-example","reason":"uw-harness flags db/migrate/001_setup.rb as a secret-looking value. It is the SHA1 hash of the default admin password 'admin', which doc/INSTALL documents and which Redmine forces users to change at first login. It is not a real secret, and the migration may not be changed, so this check stays partial."},{"requirement":"full-gate","reason":"Left out of bin/harness