aar non-ASCII test (needs the en_US.ISO8859-1 locale), bundle audit (needs network), and the PostgreSQL/MySQL and Ruby 3.3/3.4 matrix. The upstream workflows tests.yml and linters.yml still run all of them.\"},{\"requirement\":\"ci\",\"reason\":\"The uw-harness package is not published on npm (npx -y uw-harness returned 404 here), so the new harness.yml workflow will fail until it is published. The gates were checked with the local build of uw-harness (check passes) and run directly from a clean shell.\"},{\"requirement\":\"deploy-explicit\",\"reason\":\"Without human answers, docs/deploy.md and docs/observability.md keep open TODO blocks, so these two checks stay partial.\"}],\"summary\":\"The harness uses Rake, the task runner Redmine already has: new tasks in the root Rakefile, plus a bin/harness wrapper that picks a supported Ruby and bootstraps config/database.yml for SQLite3 before bundle install. From a clean shell, `bin/harness setup` works. `bin/harness check-fast` passes in about 40 s (RuboCop, Stylelint, 3383 unit and helper tests, 0 failures). `bin/harness check` passes in about 3 minutes (6296 tests plus the autoload test, 0 failures). No test was skipped, deleted or excluded, and no product code changed. One finding: `db:prepare` always fails at migration 072 on a new database, so setup uses `db:create db:migrate`. Docs, three ADRs (two inferred), four skills, AGENTS.md, a CI workflow running uw-harness verify, a pre-push hook, compose.yaml, .env.example and .tool-versions were added. Seven open questions (deploy, observability, contribution process, CI, default database, skipped tests) are TODO blocks.\",\"first_task\":{\"title\":\"Add a test for the /up health check route\",\"description\":\"config/routes.rb exposes GET /up (rails/health#show) for load balancers and uptime monitors, but no test in test/ covers it. Add a routing test and an integration test, so that a change to the routes or to authentication filters cannot break the health check without a failing test.\",\"acceptance\":[\"A new routing assertion (for example in test/integration/routing/) checks that GET /up routes to rails/health#show.\",\"A new integration test checks that an anonymous GET /up returns 200, also when the setting 'login_required' is enabled.\",\"Only files under test/ change, `bin/harness check-fast` and `bin/harness check` pass, and a dated entry is added to docs/harness/log.md.\"]}}","structured_output":{"changes":[{"path":"Rakefile","requirement":"task-runner","summary":"Kept the upstream lines. Added the harness tasks help, setup, dev, lint, check-fast, check and test-system to the root Rakefile, because uw-harness reads task names only from that file. They wrap bin/rails, RuboCop and Stylelint, and each depends on :environment so that RuboCop stays clean."},{"path":"bin/harness","requirement":"fast-gate","summary":"New wrapper. It picks a Ruby >= 3.3 and < 4.1, falling back to Homebrew Ruby when /usr/bin/ruby is too old. For setup it writes a SQLite3 config/database.yml if missing and runs bundle install and yarn install. Then it runs bundle exec rake <task>."},{"path":".github/workflows/harness.yml","requirement":"ci","summary":"New workflow on pull_request and on push to master: Ruby 4.0, Node 20, svn and hg, then npx -y uw-harness verify. Upstream tests.yml and linters.yml are unchanged."},{"path":".githooks/pre-push","requirement":"hooks","summary":"Pre-push hook that runs bin/harness check-fast. rake setup installs it with git config core.hooksPath .githooks."},{"path":"compose.yaml","requirement":"local-env","summary":"Optional PostgreSQL 14 and MySQL 8.4 services, the same as in tests.yml. The default setup uses SQLite3 and needs neither."},{"path":"docs/local-dev.md","requirement":"local-env","summary":"Prerequisites, first run, daily run, other databases, reset, debug and common problems. Also TODOs on the default database and on the tests the gates skip."},{"path":".env.example","requirement":"env-example","summary":"Lists every environment variable that the code, tests and Rake tasks read, with safe values. It also points to the git-ignored YAML config files and their .example templates."},{"path":".tool-versions","requirement":"toolchain-pinned","summary":"ruby 4.0.0 (the version the gates were verified with, also in the CI matrix) and nodejs 20 (the CI version)."},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","requirement":"architecture","summary":"The Mermaid diagram, then one section per component with folders, tech, key tables and the /up health route. Also lists what the repository does not show."},{"path":"docs/product.md","requirement":"product","summary":"Value proposition, user roles, 10 use cases with their code entry points, and a glossary."},{"path":"docs/decisions/0001-record-architecture-decisions.md","requirement":"decisions","summary":"The ADR format: context, decision, consequences, plus how to mark inferred records."},{"path":"docs/decisions/0002-multi-database-support-via-database-yml.md","requirement":"decisions","summary":"Inferred ADR: several databases are supported, and the Gemfile installs the adapter gems named in config/database.yml."},{"path":"docs/decisions/0003-importmap-stimulus-without-js-build.md","requirement":"decisions","summary":"Inferred ADR: Stimulus with importmap and Propshaft, no JavaScript build step."},{"path":"docs/agreements/working-agreements.md","requirement":"agreements","summary":"Branch and commit style taken from the git history, rules for agents, and a definition of done that includes the fast gate. Also TODOs on the contribution process and on the CI workflow."},{"path":"docs/deploy.md","requirement":"deploy-explicit","summary":"Summary of doc/INSTALL and doc/UPGRADING: environments, build, deploy, rollback and checks after a deploy. Two TODO blocks for what the repository does not show."},{"path":"docs/observability.md","requirement":"observability","summary":"Rails logger, log level and destinations, GET /up, the Admin > Information checklist, and how to tell that something is wrong. One TODO on production logs, error tracking and alerts."},{"path":"docs/harness/log.md","requirement":"implementation-log","summary":"Log header plus 'Notes from the harness build': gate timings, why the tasks are in the Rakefile, checks left out, the source of skipped tests, and the migration 072 / db:prepare finding."},{"path":".agents/skills/implement-change/SKILL.md","requirement":"skills","summary":"From task to verified change: find code and tests, run one test, check-fast, check, commit style, log entry."},{"path":".agents/skills/debug-local/SKILL.md","requirement":"skills","summary":"Reproduce, logs, debugger breakpoints, console and fixtures, SCM/LDAP skips, seeds, plugins."},{"path":".agents/skills/write-migration/SKILL.md","requirement":"skills","summary":"Portable migrations across SQLite3, PostgreSQL, MySQL and SQL Server: migrate, rollback, fixtures, compose databases."},{"path":".agents/skills/frontend-stimulus/SKILL.md","requirement":"skills","summary":"Stimulus controllers, importmap pins, CSS with open-color variables, sprite_icon and icons:generate, Stylelint, system tests."},{"path":".claude/skills","requirement":"skills","summary":"Relative symlink to ../.agents/skills."},{"path":"AGENTS.md","requirement":"agents-file","summary":"69-line index: what Redmine is, commands, layout, conventions, how to verify (check-fast before done, log entry), what never to do, links to docs and skills."},{"path":"CLAUDE.md","requirement":"agents-file","summary":"Symlink to AGENTS.md."}],"gates":{"setup":"bin/harness setup","fast":"bin/harness check-fast","full":"bin/harness check"},"todos":[{"requirement":"deploy-explicit","question":"Is this copy of Redmine deployed anywhere by your team (which server, which environments), or is it only a mirror of upstream used for development?","file":"docs/deploy.md"},{"requirement":"deploy-explicit","question":"If this copy is deployed: who can deploy, how is a release bui